.TH PROTOPEEK 1 "August 2026" "ProtoPeek 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
protopeek \- open the local ProtoPeek gRPC and HTTP workbench
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B protopeek
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B protopeek
.RI [ options ]
.I target
.br
.B protopeek download
.RI [ --output " NAME" ]
.RI [ --sha256 " 64_HEX" ]
.I URL
.br
.B protopeek migrate-gobarry
.RI [ --apply ]
.RI [ --preferences= bool ]
.RI [ --session= bool ]
.br
.B protopeek migrate-gobarry
.BI --rollback " RECEIPT_ID"
.SH DESCRIPTION
ProtoPeek starts an unauthenticated local web workbench. With no target it opens
the Protocol Peek dashboard. An exact host:port connects directly to that gRPC
target. A bare host opens the dashboard's visible scan and checks only port
50051 with plaintext and port 443 with verified TLS. An HTTP(S) authority checks
its stated or default port. Overview, Protocols, Network, Downloader, Security,
and Settings are the six primary local browser areas.
.PP
The listener binds to 127.0.0.1 by default. Do not expose it to an untrusted
network. For a container published only on host loopback,
.B \-allow-non-loopback-bind
permits the container-interface listener while retaining the loopback request
Host and Origin policy. The separate
.B \-unsafe-allow-remote
option accepts non-loopback browser Hosts and requires an external TLS,
authentication, and rate-limit boundary.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-help
Print the complete command-line reference and exit.
.TP
.B \-version
Print the installed version and exit.
.TP
.B \-plaintext
Use unencrypted HTTP/2 for the target gRPC connection.
.TP
.B \-insecure
Use TLS without verifying the server certificate or name. This is not secure
and cannot be combined with
.BR \-plaintext .
.TP
.BI \-cacert " file"
Trust roots from a PEM certificate file.
.TP
.BI \-cert " file"
Present a PEM client certificate. Must be used with
.BR \-key .
.TP
.BI \-key " file"
Use the PEM private key for
.BR \-cert .
.TP
.BI \-authority " name"
Set the HTTP/2 authority and TLS verification name.
.TP
.BI \-proto " file"
Load a protobuf source file instead of relying only on reflection. May be
specified more than once.
.TP
.BI \-protoset " file"
Load an encoded FileDescriptorSet. May be specified more than once.
.TP
.BI \-import-path " directory"
Add a protobuf import directory.
.TP
.BI \-H " name:value"
Add metadata to reflection and RPC requests. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-rpc-header " name:value"
Add metadata only to RPC invocations.
.TP
.BI \-reflect-header " name:value"
Add metadata only to reflection requests.
.TP
.BI \-connect-timeout " seconds"
Limit initial connection time.
.TP
.BI \-max-time " seconds"
Set the ProtoPeek-owned local wall for one ordinary RPC invocation. When the
wall is reached, return bounded partial evidence without presenting local
cancellation as a server gRPC status. Zero or a value above 60 seconds uses the
built-in 60-second safety wall.
.TP
.BI \-bind " address"
Bind the browser listener. Defaults to 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.B \-allow-non-loopback-bind
Permit a non-loopback container listener while still accepting browser
requests only for loopback Hosts and matching Origins. Use only when the outer
container port is published on host loopback.
.TP
.BI \-port " port"
Choose the browser listener port. Zero selects an available port.
.TP
.BI \-open-browser= bool
Enable or disable automatic browser opening.
.TP
.B \-unsafe-allow-remote
Permit a non-loopback browser listener and accept non-loopback browser Hosts.
The listener has no built-in user authentication; use only behind an explicit
TLS, authentication, and rate-limit boundary.
.SH DOWNLOADER COMMAND
The
.B download
subcommand ships in ProtoPeek v0.5.0. Homebrew and Scoop remain at v0.4.0 until
their separate dependency-aware package updates pass, so those package-manager
installs do not provide this command yet.
.PP
It accepts exactly one absolute HTTP(S) URL without user information and uses
an explicitly configured or system-installed
.BR aria2c .
ProtoPeek does not bundle aria2. URL fragments are ignored.
.TP
.BI --output " NAME"
Use one safe output filename, at most 255 characters, with no directory
components.
.TP
.BI --sha256 " 64_HEX"
Require an exact 64-hexadecimal-character SHA-256 digest. A completed transfer
without verified matching checksum evidence fails.
.PP
The command uses the same host configuration and aria2 session files as the
browser UI, but owns a separate local engine process and does not attach to an
already-running ProtoPeek process. If another process owns the engine lock, the
command refuses to start and explains how to retry.
.PP
Progress is written to standard error and only the completed output path is
written to standard output. Interrupting the command returns status 130 and
preserves partial data plus the aria2 session for later resumption. Shutdown is
bounded to five seconds.
.SH GOBARRYGO MIGRATION COMMAND
The
.B migrate-gobarry
subcommand ships in ProtoPeek v0.5.0. With no mutation flag it performs an
observational preview of the one known GoBarryGo local profile. It does not
accept an arbitrary source path, start aria2, or write either product's state.
.TP
.B --apply
Copy the selected compatible preferences and resumable aria2 session into
ProtoPeek after displaying the preview. Source files are never deleted,
renamed, uninstalled, or rewritten. Imported session jobs remain paused.
.TP
.BI --preferences= bool
Include compatible GoBarryGo preferences. Defaults to true. Use
.B --preferences=false
for a session-only import.
.TP
.BI --session= bool
Include the bounded resumable aria2 session. Defaults to true. Use
.B --session=false
for a preferences-only import.
.TP
.BI --rollback " RECEIPT_ID"
Restore the exact ProtoPeek state recorded before one import. Rollback refuses
if the current target configuration, session, or migration ledger no longer
matches that receipt, so newer work is not overwritten.
.PP
Import and rollback require the ProtoPeek Downloader to be stopped. For the
final preview and import, stop GoBarryGo as well so its source snapshot remains
stable. Successful imports store private mode-0600 state, a source-hash ledger,
and a guarded rollback receipt. Repeating an identical import is idempotent.
Unsupported GoBarryGo behavior, including native completion/error
notifications, is reported but not silently claimed as migrated.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Open the Protocol Peek dashboard:
.B protopeek
.TP
Probe the bounded candidates for a bare host in the visible scan:
.B protopeek localhost
.TP
Connect to a plaintext local gRPC server:
.B protopeek \-plaintext localhost:50051
.TP
Start without opening a browser:
.B protopeek \-open-browser=false
.TP
Download one file with checksum evidence:
.B protopeek download --output artifact.bin --sha256 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef https://example.test/artifact.bin
.TP
Preview the GoBarryGo bridge without writing:
.B protopeek migrate-gobarry
.TP
Copy compatible preferences and session after reviewing the preview:
.B protopeek migrate-gobarry --apply
.TP
Guardedly restore a recorded pre-import state:
.B protopeek migrate-gobarry --rollback RECEIPT_ID
.SH STATE
Saved targets, requests, and workspace settings are stored in the local browser
profile. Automatic history and default exports redact known credential fields,
but exported debugging data should still be reviewed before sharing.
.SH ALIAS
.B pp
is an identical executable entrypoint. If another program already owns that
name, use
.B protopeek
instead.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pp (1),
the project documentation at https://protopeek.shreyam1008.com.np/docs/
